  "description": "Participants are randomly assigned to one of two greenery styles (plants built into furniture, or climbing plants on structures). They then see six rendered rooms in random order: a living room and a bedroom, each without plants, with potted plants and with integrated greenery. For every room they rate four perceived-restorativeness items and seven adjectives on 1–7 scales. Rebuilt from Bellini, Miola, Sperduti, Caccaro, Pinton, Graffeo & Pazzaglia (2025), Frontiers in Psychology 16: 1631417, using the 12 renderings printed in Figures 1–2 of the paper (CC BY 4.0).",
  "logoPosition": "right",
